# The two things a node's detail says that are not sentences: a verb's disc and a fact's bubble.
#
# The screen this replaced said both in ink alone. Every action row drew its label in the
# accent, so a card of eleven verbs was a wall of one colour with the row that deletes something
# somewhere inside it; and every fact was a grey label beside a white value, so "verified" and
# "Echo Repeater" were the same kind of answer typographically and the difference between a key
# somebody proved and one nobody has was one of two inks on two words.
#
# What to watch is that the colour has moved twice, and in opposite directions. Out of the verbs'
# words and into a container at their leading edge - so the labels read as a column of labels and
# the two rows that cost something are the only coloured words on the card. And into a shape
# around the values that are *states*, which is the handful of rows a reader is checking rather
# than reading: a filled capsule for a state worth reporting, an outlined one for the state a
# thing is normally in.
#
# The two marks are now on two screens - the discs on the node's verbs, the capsules on its
# detail - which is what this walks through.
#
# Delta Camp is the node worth opening because it arrived over MQTT rather than over the air,
# which is the one fact on the Signal card that quietly invalidates the three above it.

scene demo
clock 2026-01-15 12:00
verified DLTA
tab nodes
# The Nodes list has four rows before its first node - the filter row, the sort row, the Map and
# Waypoints (MESH_UI_NODES_LEAD_ROWS) - so a node's row is its index in the demo roster plus
# four. Delta Camp is seeds[4] and row 8.
key down 8
key a
hold 1400

# In to the verbs. Discs down the leading edge, ordinary ink in the words, and the two rows that
# are not ordinary - ignore in the warning family, remove in the error family - saying so in both
# places at once.
key a
hold 1000
key down 6
hold 1400

# Back out to the detail, and on to Identity: the row the whole screen is qualified by, a key
# this node proved in person, as a filled capsule rather than as a green word.
key b
key right
hold 1600

# Signal, where "MQTT" is the qualifier on the SNR and the hop count above it. The neutral state -
# a node heard over the air - is the outlined capsule this one is not wearing.
key right
hold 1600

# The same two marks in every theme. A disc is a family's container and a chip is a row's tone, so
# nothing here is switched by hand: the colourblind palette moves the accent and the verdicts
# without a renderer knowing a palette exists, and on the contrast theme the outline is the whole
# of what says a neutral state is a state at all.
theme light
hold 1400
theme contrast
hold 1400
theme colorblind
hold 1800
